/-!
# Minimal offenders and the Fitting subgroup

Source: Aschbacher--Smith, *The Classification of Quasithin Groups*,
D.2.13--14 and the reductions D.2.18--21, printed pp.184--188.
The preliminary modules prove the faithful Fitting action and D.2.18,
D.2.20 and D.2.21. The cyclic branch of D.2.13 includes the actual
order-three and order-five support decompositions. The noncyclic reduction
proves faithful restriction and strict ratio drop on hyperplane fixed
spaces, and establishes all of D.2.13(4). The elementary-core and configuration modules retain their
explicit preceding-source premises; full D.2.13--14 and D.2.19 are not
asserted by this partial assembly.
-/
